cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in a publication, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dsgelab: a general toolkit for solving DSGE models in Python"
abstract: >-
  Steady state, Klein/QZ first-order solution, second-order perturbation and a partial third order (the cubic block and the risk slope), Chebyshev projection, perfect foresight with expectation errors, optimal policy (Ramsey, discretion, optimal simple rules) and welfare, Kalman filtering and smoothing, Bayesian estimation, shock decompositions and forecasts, reading Dynare .mod files, and export to Dynare and MacroModelling.jl. Validated against Dynare, MacroModelling.jl and closed-form solutions.
authors:
  - family-names: "Moreira"
    given-names: "Gustavo Hoffmann"
    email: "gustavo@gakusai.net"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0827-2521"
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"   # set to the release day when tagging v0.5.0
license: MIT
# The DOI is filled in with the first release archived on Zenodo, which makes the citation stable,
# since a repository URL is not an archivable reference.
repository-code: "https://github.com/GustavoHM/dsgelab"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
keywords:
  - "DSGE"
  - "perturbation"
  - "rational expectations"
  - "Python"
